Z||000000||bHooper||05-15-2000||11:15 AM||||Does anyone (with any experience at this) have any good tips on reataching the body work?<P>The parts I think might give me some trouble, are the ones that were attached with the large rivits, such as the fenders, qtr panels, and ground effects.  I do not have a desire to purchase the specific, $600 rivit gun for this job.  <P>Also, the bumper supports used some funky plastic "bolts" to hold things to the subframe.  Is there a good substitute for these?<P>Has anyone done this b4?<P>thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||4
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-15-2000||11:55 AM||||Pop rivets can be used for GFX.  Get one for under 20 bucks.  The fenders are easy.  They should have only bolts.  Not sure about the bupersupport... I left the whole bumper off my GT for now.  ||||reg||1
